## Drumpad Feature -- Full Implementation Plan

### 1. Architecture Overview

The drumpad feature is a standalone free-play instrument page at `/drumpad`. Unlike the existing `/live` page (which is about timing accuracy against a pattern), the drumpad page is a creative/performance tool inspired by hardware MPC/Launchpad controllers. It has its own dedicated Zustand store, its own keyboard handler hook, and a self-contained recording/playback engine that does not depend on the existing `Scheduler` class.

**Why a separate store rather than extending `useLivePracticeStore`:** The live practice store is tightly coupled to pattern matching, timing grading, and session statistics. The drumpad has fundamentally different concerns: recording timestamped hit sequences, loop playback, choke groups, and kit switching. Mixing these into the live practice store would create confusing conditional logic and bloat. A new `useDrumpadStore` keeps each feature cleanly scoped.

### 2. Solving the 16-Pad Problem with 9 Sounds

The existing `DrumSynth.ts` has 9 `InstrumentId` values. To fill a 4x4 grid (16 pads), introduce 7 variants that reuse the existing synth functions with modified parameters. The approach is a new concept called `PadVoice`, which wraps an `InstrumentId` with optional pitch/velocity/decay overrides.

The 16-pad mapping:

| Row | Pad 0 | Pad 1 | Pad 2 | Pad 3 |
|-----|-------|-------|-------|-------|
| 0 (top) | Crash | Ride | Hi-Hat Open | Hi-Hat Closed |
| 1 | Tom High | Tom Mid | Tom Low | Rimshot (snare variant, low velocity, higher pitch) |
| 2 | Snare | Clap (snare variant, wider noise band) | Sidestick (snare variant, very short, high-pass) | Cross-stick (snare variant) |
| 3 (bottom) | Kick | Kick Deep (lower pitch variant) | Sub Kick (sine only, very low) | Percussion (tom variant, very high pitch, short) |

The 7 extra voices are implemented as a new `playPadVoice` function in a new file `/src/lib/audio/PadVoices.ts`. This function takes a `PadVoiceId` (a union of the 9 original `InstrumentId` values plus 7 new string IDs) and calls the underlying Web Audio API with modified parameters, or delegates to `playInstrument` for the original 9. This avoids modifying `DrumSynth.ts`.

Concrete `PadVoiceId` type:

```typescript
export type PadVoiceId =
  | InstrumentId                    // 9 original sounds
  | 'kick-deep'                     // kick with lower pitch sweep (start 100Hz)
  | 'kick-sub'                      // kick sine-only body, no click oscillator
  | 'snare-clap'                    // layered noise bursts to simulate clap
  | 'snare-rimshot'                 // snare body only, higher pitch (250Hz), short decay
  | 'snare-sidestick'               // very short click, high-pass filtered
  | 'snare-cross'                   // snare with bandpass, muted character
  | 'percussion'                    // tom at 350Hz with 0.08s decay
```

### 3. Component Hierarchy

```
/src/app/drumpad/page.tsx              -- Page component (route entry)
  <Header />                           -- Existing, modified to include Drumpad nav
  <DrumpadPage />                      -- Main client component
    <PadGrid />                        -- 4x4 grid of DrumPad components
      <DrumPad />                      -- Individual pad (16 instances)
    <DrumpadControls />                -- Transport-like controls panel
      <RecordButton />                 -- Toggle recording
      <PlaybackButton />               -- Play/stop loop
      <LoopToggle />                   -- Enable/disable looping
      <BpmSlider />                    -- Playback speed control
      <ClearButton />                  -- Clear recording
      <KitSelector />                  -- Switch between sound kits
    <RecordingTimeline />              -- Visual display of recorded hits
    <VolumeControl />                  -- Master volume (reuse existing component)
```

### 4. New Files to Create

**Route:**
- `/src/app/drumpad/page.tsx` -- Page entry point with `'use client'` and `<Header />`

**Components (new directory: `/src/components/drumpad/`):**
- `DrumpadPage.tsx` -- Main container, wires up keyboard handler, manages layout
- `PadGrid.tsx` -- Renders 4x4 CSS Grid of `DrumPad` components
- `DrumPad.tsx` -- Single pad with visual feedback, touch/mouse/keyboard support
- `DrumpadControls.tsx` -- Recording transport controls, kit selector, BPM
- `RecordingTimeline.tsx` -- Horizontal timeline showing recorded hits as colored dots

**Audio:**
- `/src/lib/audio/PadVoices.ts` -- `PadVoiceId` type, `playPadVoice()` function, `PAD_VOICE_CONFIG` constant, and synthesis functions for the 7 new variant sounds

**State:**
- `/src/lib/store/useDrumpadStore.ts` -- Zustand store for drumpad state

**Hook:**
- `/src/lib/hooks/useDrumpadKeyboard.ts` -- Keyboard event handler for drumpad pads

**Types/config:**
- `/src/lib/drumpad/types.ts` -- All drumpad-specific types, constants, pad configurations, keyboard mappings, choke groups, and kit definitions

### 5. Existing Files to Modify

- `/src/components/Header.tsx` -- Add `{ href: '/drumpad', label: 'Drumpad' }` to the `drums` section nav array
- No other existing files need modification. The feature is fully additive.

### 6. State Management: `useDrumpadStore.ts`

```typescript
import { create } from 'zustand';

// --- Types defined in /src/lib/drumpad/types.ts ---

interface RecordedHit {
  padId: PadVoiceId;
  timestamp: number;        // Relative to recording start (in seconds)
  velocity: number;
}

interface DrumpadState {
  // Active pads (for visual feedback)
  activePads: Set<PadVoiceId>;

  // Current kit index (0-3, like Launchpad's 4 sound chains)
  currentKit: number;

  // Recording
  isRecording: boolean;
  recordingStartTime: number | null;
  recordedHits: RecordedHit[];

  // Playback
  isPlaying: boolean;
  isLooping: boolean;
  playbackBpm: number;           // 100 = original speed, 50 = half, 200 = double
  playbackTimerIds: number[];    // setTimeout IDs for cancellation

  // Actions
  triggerPad: (padId: PadVoiceId, velocity?: number) => void;
  releasePad: (padId: PadVoiceId) => void;
  setKit: (index: number) => void;

  startRecording: () => void;
  stopRecording: () => void;
  clearRecording: () => void;

  startPlayback: () => void;
  stopPlayback: () => void;
  toggleLoop: () => void;
  setPlaybackBpm: (bpm: number) => void;
}
```

Key implementation details for the store:

**`triggerPad` action:** This is the central action called by both keyboard and touch/mouse. It:
1. Adds `padId` to `activePads` (visual feedback)
2. Calls `playPadVoice(padId, audioEngine.currentTime, velocity, 0.8)`
3. Handles choke groups: if `padId` is `'hihat-closed'`, it stops any currently playing `'hihat-open'` voice. This is implemented by tracking active `GainNode` references for chokeable voices in a `Map<PadVoiceId, GainNode>` inside `PadVoices.ts`, and calling `gain.gain.cancelScheduledValues()` + immediate ramp to 0.
4. If recording, pushes a `RecordedHit` with `timestamp = audioEngine.currentTime - recordingStartTime`

**`releasePad` action:** Removes `padId` from `activePads`. (In a future "hold-to-play" mode, this could also stop the sound.)

**Recording playback:** `startPlayback` reads `recordedHits`, calculates time-scaled positions based on `playbackBpm` (100 = 1x speed), and uses `setTimeout` for each hit. The `setTimeout` IDs are stored in `playbackTimerIds` so `stopPlayback` can clear them all. If `isLooping`, when the last hit plays, it schedules a new round. The loop length is `Math.ceil(recordedHits[last].timestamp)` rounded up to the nearest beat boundary.

### 7. Choke Groups

Defined as a constant in `/src/lib/drumpad/types.ts`:

```typescript
export const CHOKE_GROUPS: PadVoiceId[][] = [
  ['hihat-closed', 'hihat-open'],  // Closed chokes open
];

// Direction: later in the group chokes earlier
// hihat-closed (index 0) chokes hihat-open (index 1)
// This means: when hihat-closed triggers, any active hihat-open is silenced
```

Implementation in `PadVoices.ts`: maintain a `Map<string, GainNode>` called `activeChokeableVoices`. When a pad in a choke group triggers, look up the choke group, find any other active voices in the same group, and ramp their gain to 0 in ~5ms. Then register the new voice's gain node. On natural decay, clean up the reference.

### 8. Keyboard Mapping

4 rows x 4 columns mapped to keyboard rows, defined in `/src/lib/drumpad/types.ts`:

```typescript
export interface PadConfig {
  id: PadVoiceId;
  label: string;           // Display name on pad
  shortLabel: string;       // Abbreviated for small screens
  keyCode: string;          // KeyboardEvent.code
  keyLabel: string;         // Display on pad
  color: string;            // Tailwind border/glow color class
  row: number;
  col: number;
}

export const PAD_CONFIGS: PadConfig[] = [
  // Row 0 (top) - Cymbals: keys 1-4
